  "body": "Closes #1358\nClaim: cloud/i1358-sonnet\nAuthor model: Sonnet 5.5 (cloud/i1358-sonnet)\nReviewer model: Opus 5.5 (claude-opus-5-5)\n\n**Problem.** Light-mode secondary texts of the reader under WCAG AA, found by the Opus review of #1355: the folded blocked quote header in a moderation message (`--secondary` on `--modo`, 4.23:1) and the date of an allowlisted continuation (75 % opacity), 3.28:1 classic (3.01 modern). Review also found the folded quote header of any continuation at 3.0–3.4.\n\n**Cause.** `--secondary` is too light on the `--modo` tint; a continuation's `opacity: .75` fades text and surface together, and only dark had the page-text override for its date and note (#1210).\n\n**Change** (`reader.css`, no other theme touched):\n- `.message.mode`: `--secondary-tinted` (80 % secondary, 20 % text, as #1355) on the folded quote header → 5.39:1 light, 5.19 dark.\n- Light only: date and note of a continuation in `--text` (the colour dark already uses) → 6.4–7.3:1.\n- Folded quote header of a continuation in `--text`, both modes → 6.2–8.0:1.\n- Not covered: other `--secondary` texts of a continuation (ordinary quote header, signature, trailer): follow-up #1360.\n\n**Tests.** `ReaderAllowlistContrastWebTests` (app-hosted, macOS CI): the probe now composites a continuation's opacity onto the page; 16 new tests (moderation quote header, allowlisted continuation, plain continuation × modern/classic × light/dark). They cannot run on Linux; pre-fix values (4.23, 3.28, 3.01, …) and post-fix values were computed with the sheet's tokens, and each new test has an expectation that fails before the change. Opus review: 3 rounds, APPROVE on 423b471.\n\nDevice check owed: none beyond the hosted tests.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_014QH2CG5AxYHauqLdEG5ACC",
