   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** (head bc0d291)\n\n1. **High**, `ReaderAllowlistContrastWebTests.swift:112` and `:119`. Does not compile: `guard let seen else { return Issue.record(\"…\") }` in a `Void` function (`unexpected non-void return value in void function`, swiftc 6.2.4, language mode 6). Fix: `{ Issue.record(\"…\"); return }`.\n2. **Medium**, `reader.css:326-332`. Covers one case of a wider class; other continuations are left out with no issue. Recomputed (light unless marked): normal continuation date 3.06 modern / 2.73 classic; `.continuation-note` 3.15; folded quote header in an allowlisted continuation 3.05 classic / 3.28 modern (`checkContinuation` reads `seen[1]` but never asserts); in a moderation continuation 3.15; in a normal continuation, dark, 3.39. Fix: widen the rule or open a follow-up issue.\n3. **Detail**, `reader.css:326`. The comment says \"two more light cases\" but the `.message.mode` rule also fixes dark (4.30 → 5.19); say so.\n\nRecomputed: moderation light 4.23 → 5.39; allowlisted continuation date classic light 3.28 → 6.63, modern 3.01 → 7.12; dark keeps `--text`. New rule has the same specificity as the classic header rule and comes later. `.mode` and `.whitelist` never apply together. `fade` model is right. Existing 4 tests unchanged.\n\nRound 1 fixes (one commit): 1 fixed; 2 fixed by widening (light date/note of every continuation in `--text`, quote header of every continuation in `--text`, new plain-continuation tests, `seen[1]` asserted); 3 comment rewritten.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
