   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5, round 2): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 9571f08\n\n1. **Medium**, `reader.css:327-335`. The class is only partly fixed and the comment claims more than the code does. The 75 % fade pulls every `--secondary` text in a continuation below 4.5:1; only the date, the note and the folded quote header were raised. Still low: ordinary quote header (\"X a écrit\", `b.s1`) 3.15:1 light / 3.61 dark; signature and trailer 3.15 / 3.61; ordinary quote header in a moderation continuation 2.89 / 3.35. Fix: one rule for the whole class (measured) plus a test, or narrow the comment and open a follow-up issue listing these cases.\n2. **Detail**, `ReaderAllowlistContrastWebTests.swift:7-9`. The suite doc comment still describes only #644.\n\nChecked by the reviewer: cascade and specificity correct (light-only date rule wins over the classic whitelist date; continuation quote rule wins over whitelist/mode rules; classic dark date untouched); ratios recomputed (moderation 4.23→5.39 light, 4.30→5.19 dark; continuation date 2.73–3.28 → 6.46–7.26; continuation folded quote header → 6.18–8.04); each new test has an expectation that fails before the fix; round-1 compile error fixed (typecheck with swiftc `-swift-version 6` passes, swiftlint 0 violations). Hosted WebKit tests not run (need Mac/CI).\n\nRound 2 fixes (one commit): 1 — narrowed the comment to what is fixed and opened follow-up #1360 (other secondary texts of a continuation: same class, wider than #1358's two named cases and its tests); 2 — suite doc comment updated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
